/-! # Function norms of finite locally free morphisms

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 0BD2 and Section 0BCX, conditions (1) and (2)
(blueprint: lem-sfb-finite-locally-free-function-norm).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The matrix of multiplication by a section in a basis for the module structure
induced by the scheme morphism on sections.

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, proof of Tag 0BD2
(blueprint: lem-sfb-finite-locally-free-function-norm). -/
noncomputable def Scheme.Hom.sectionMultiplicationMatrix
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ X) (U : X.Opens) (d : ℕ)
    (e : @Module.Basis (Fin d) Γ(X, U) Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ U)
      inferInstance inferInstance (f.app U).hom.toModule)
    (b : Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ U)) : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) Γ(X, U) :=
  letI := (f.app U).hom.toModule
  fun i j ↦ e.repr (b * e j) i

/-- A finite locally free morphism of positive constant degree has a multiplicative,
restriction-compatible norm of functions, with the scalar-power and residue-field
vanishing properties, characterized by local multiplication determinants in every basis.

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 0BD2 and Section 0BCX
(blueprint: lem-sfb-finite-locally-free-function-norm).

Proof:
1. By lem-pc-flf-properties the pushforward of the structure sheaf is locally free of
   rank d. Use def-amb-finite-locally-free-module and def-pc-scheme to refine its
   trivializations to affine opens inside the given V. Their inverse images are affine
   by def-weil-finite-integral-morphism; no finite cover is required.
2. Apply lem-a1-principal-free-algebra-determinant-norm on each chart, using the singleton
   principal cover generated by 1. Its affine restriction clause and basis independence
   from def-weil-endomorphism-determinant compare all smaller affine charts.
3. On overlaps refine by affine opens and compare determinants. The structure-sheaf
   axioms in def-pc-scheme glue the compatible local norms uniquely. Comparing refinements
   shows independence of the cover and the determinant formula on every free affine chart.
   The empty cover gives the unique section over the empty open.
4. Compute both sides of restriction compatibility on free affine charts of the smaller
   open. Their local determinant formulas agree, so the sheaf equality axiom applies.
5. Multiplication endomorphisms satisfy m_bc = m_b composed with m_c. The determinant
   identities lem-sfb-matrix-cramer-determinant-identities imply multiplicativity.
   The permutation formula def-weil-pbc-matrix-determinant gives det(I) = 1 and
   det(a I) = a^d. Check these identities on the affine cover and glue.
6. For y over x use an affine free chart Spec D over Spec R. Evaluation into the residue
   field has kernel the corresponding prime q, by def-weil-residue-field and
   def-weil-affine-spectrum. If b belongs to q, lem-pd-finite-free-norm-prime-criterion
   puts its norm in the contracted prime p. Thus its value in the residue field at x
   vanishes. This argument requires no reducedness, separability or Noetherian condition.
-/
theorem exists_finiteLocallyFree_functionNorm
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ X) (d : ℕ) (hd : 1 ≤ d)
    [f.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfDegree d] :
    ∃ ν : ∀ V : X.Opens, Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ V) →* Γ(X, V),
      (∀ (V W : X.Opens) (hWV : W ≤ V) (b : Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ V)),
        X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op (ν V b) =
          ν W (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (f.preimage_mono hWV)).op b)) ∧
      (∀ (V : X.Opens) (a : Γ(X, V)), ν V (f.app V a) = a ^ d) ∧
      (∀ (V : X.Opens) (b : Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ V)) (y : Y) (hy : y ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V),
        Y.evaluation (f ⁻¹ᵁ V) y hy b = 0 → X.evaluation V (f y) hy (ν V b) = 0) ∧
      (∀ (V U : X.Opens) (hUV : U ≤ V), IsAffineOpen U →
        ∀ (e : @Module.Basis (Fin d) Γ(X, U) Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ U)
          inferInstance inferInstance (f.app U).hom.toModule) (b : Γ(Y, f ⁻¹ᵁ V)),
        X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUV).op (ν V b) =
          Matrix.det (f.sectionMultiplicationMatrix U d e
            (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (f.preimage_mono hUV)).op b))) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
